# Punctuation Standards

## Em Dash (—) is banned

Never use the em dash character (—) in any copy, JSX, strings, or comments.

### Replacements

| Instead of | Use |
|-----------|-----|
| `word — word` | `word. Word` (split into two sentences) |
| `building — check back` | `building. Check back` |
| `from the logo — to the palette` | `from the logo to the palette` (just remove it) |
| `Title — subtitle` | `Title: subtitle` (use a colon) |

### Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<span>Currently coding this portfolio — check back soon.</span>

// ✅ GOOD
<span>Currently coding this portfolio. Check back soon.</span>
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
note: "Helped shape this site — from logo to palette."

// ✅ GOOD
note: "Helped shape this site, from logo to palette."
```
